Backport-of: https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/pull/5013 (commit e17c0d9f0)
fix(hyprland/workspaces): adapt dispatch commands for Lua IPC protocol

Hyprland 0.54 replaced the text-based dispatch socket protocol with a
Lua-based one. Waybar 0.15.0's Workspace::handleClicked sends legacy
bare-arg strings ("dispatch workspace N") to the IPC socket, which
Hyprland >= 0.54 parses as invalid Lua and rejects silently — clicking
a workspace button does nothing while keyboard binds keep working
(binds go through the Lua config, not the socket).

This backport of upstream PR #5013 adds IPC::dispatch() which probes
the running Hyprland once and routes through the Lua hl.dsp API when
detected, falling back to legacy text otherwise, and points
Workspace::handleClicked at it for workspace /
focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor / togglespecialworkspace.

The upstream PR also patches Workspaces::handleScroll; that method
does not exist in 0.15.0, so it is skipped here.

Drop this patch once waybar ships a release containing PR #5013.

